<section class="cx-section cx-spotlight" id="daycare-compliance" style="background:var(--dark)">
  <div class="cx-container">
    <div class="r" style="max-width:720px">
      <div class="cx-eyebrow">Regulatory Compliance</div>
      <h2 class="cx-h2">Three inspections every<br>daycare renovation must pass.</h2>
      <p class="cx-sub" style="margin-top:16px">Licensed childcare facilities in Ontario face overlapping regulatory requirements. VNG is familiar with all three and builds to satisfy each simultaneously, so you are not going back to make changes after one inspector clears you and another does not.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-cost-factors stagger" style="margin-top:48px">
      <div class="cx-cost-factor r">
        <h3>Ontario Building Code, Group A Occupancy</h3>
        <p>Childcare centres are classified as Group A, Division 2 assembly occupancy under the OBC. This triggers requirements for egress, fire separation, occupant load calculations, accessibility, and washroom counts that differ significantly from office or retail occupancy. We build to these standards from day one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-cost-factor r">
        <h3>CCEYA Physical Environment Requirements</h3>
        <p>The Child Care and Early Years Act specifies minimum floor areas per child by age group, washroom ratios, sleep room provisions, outdoor play area access, and safe materials. The Ministry of Education licensing inspector reviews compliance with these requirements separately from the building permit inspection.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-cost-factor r">
        <h3>Municipal Zoning &amp; Change-of-Use</h3>
        <p>Many daycare locations require a change-of-use permit from the previous occupancy. VNG manages the full change-of-use process including coordinating architect drawings, submitting applications, and responding to plan examiner comments across all GTA municipalities.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-cost-factor r">
        <h3>Fire Code &amp; Emergency Egress</h3>
        <p>Licensed childcare facilities require compliant emergency egress routes, emergency lighting, fire alarm systems, and fire suppression provisions appropriate to the occupancy and building type. We coordinate with your fire code consultant and local fire marshal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

